<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila buys 25,000 tonnes U.S. white corn.</title>
<headline>Manila buys 25,000 tonnes U.S. white corn.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' National Food Authority (NFA) on Wednesday bought 25,000 tonnes of U.S. white corn at $201.8 per tonne, an NFA official said.</p>
<p>The corn will be bought through the Continental Grains Co which won the bidding, NFA Administrator Eduardo Gomez said.  </p>
<p>Gomez also said the white corn would be milled into corn grits for human consumption.</p>
